% Test cases for the mechanical in-exsufflation policy
% (mechanical_insufflation.le): synthetic claims, one or two per criterion
% of LCD L33795 and per payment condition of dmepos.le and Policy Article
% A52510. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's or the
% Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer conditional. The
% queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query, so "stage" reads
% its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary, and what minimal
% change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base mechanical_insufflation cases includes these resources:
    mechanical_insufflation.

the knowledge base mechanical_insufflation cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for the device (E0482): amyotrophic lateral
% sclerosis (G12.21, on the Article's list), the treating practitioner's
% finding on the impairment, and every documentation requirement in the
% record. E0482 is not on the CMS face-to-face list: the order need only
% reach the supplier before the date of service.
scenario als_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the cough assist device.
    the HCPCS code of the cough assist device is "E0482".
    the cough assist device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "G12.21".
    the finding neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "forced vital capacity 38 percent of predicted and a peak cough flow of 140 litres per minute; cannot raise secretions during chest infections".
    the order for the cough assist device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the cough assist device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the cough assist device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the cough assist device includes order date.
    the order for the cough assist device includes description of the item.
    the order for the cough assist device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the cough assist device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the cough assist device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the cough assist device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the cough assist device.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The diagnosis on the claim is COPD (J44.1), not a neuromuscular disease of
% the list: criterion 1 fails, whatever the finding.
scenario diagnosis_not_listed is:
    claim 1 is for the cough assist device.
    the HCPCS code of the cough assist device is "E0482".
    the cough assist device is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the diagnosis code of Ben is "J44.1".
    the finding neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Duchenne muscular dystrophy (G71.01), and nothing recorded about the
% impairment: the answer is conditional on that finding alone.
scenario no_impairment_finding is:
    claim 1 is for the cough assist device.
    the HCPCS code of the cough assist device is "E0482".
    the cough assist device is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the diagnosis code of Cy is "G71.01".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance about Cy is established"].

% The Council finds the record does not show an inability to clear
% secretions: the claim is not reasonable and necessary.
scenario council_impairment_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the cough assist device.
    the HCPCS code of the cough assist device is "E0482".
    the cough assist device is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "G35.D".
    the finding neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance about Dee is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the physician's note records multiple sclerosis and fatigue; no measurement of respiratory muscle strength or cough and no episode of retained secretions appears in the record".
    rn expects answers [].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy, and the flip adds the missing proof.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the cough assist device.
    the HCPCS code of the cough assist device is "E0482".
    the cough assist device is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "G12.21".
    the finding neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the cough assist device is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the cough assist device is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the cough assist device includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the cough assist device includes order date.
    the order for the cough assist device includes description of the item.
    the order for the cough assist device includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the cough assist device includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the cough assist device was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the cough assist device was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the cough assist device"]].

% Replacement interfaces (A7020): one for Ann's own device, with its
% documentation, is payable; one for a device Eve rents is reasonable and
% necessary but not payable (Policy Article A52510).
scenario replacement_interfaces is:
    claim 1 is for the interface.
    the HCPCS code of the interface is "A7020".
    the interface is furnished to Ann.
    the interface is an accessory of the cough assist device.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-09-01.
    the HCPCS code of the cough assist device is "E0482".
    the cough assist device is furnished to Ann.
    the cough assist device is owned by the beneficiary.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "G12.21".
    the finding neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the interface is dated 2026-08-20.
    the order for the interface is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the interface includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the interface includes order date.
    the order for the interface includes description of the item.
    the order for the interface includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the interface includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the interface was communicated to the supplier on 2026-08-22.
    the interface was delivered on 2026-09-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the interface.
    claim 2 is for the second interface.
    the HCPCS code of the second interface is "A7020".
    the second interface is furnished to Eve.
    the second interface is an accessory of the rented device.
    the residence of Eve is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-09-01.
    the HCPCS code of the rented device is "E0482".
    the rented device is furnished to Eve.
    the diagnosis code of Eve is "G71.11".
    the finding neuromuscular impairment prevents secretion clearance about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the second interface is dated 2026-08-20.
    the order for the second interface is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the second interface includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the second interface includes order date.
    the order for the second interface includes description of the item.
    the order for the second interface includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the second interface includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the second interface was communicated to the supplier on 2026-08-22.
    the second interface was delivered on 2026-09-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the second interface.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].
